message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a “rotating card” that spins around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that gives perspective to the card */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  perspective: 800px;          /* Creates a 3‑D space */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Optional: content inside the card (front/back) */
.card-content {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide back side when rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

.card-back {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Place back side behind front */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="card-content">
      <h2>Front</h2>
      <p>Hover over me!</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="card-content card-back">
      <h2>Back</h2>
      <p>Thanks for hovering.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Property | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `perspective` | Gives the container a 3‑D depth so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3‑D space during transformation. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each side when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transition: transform 0.6s ease` | Animates the rotation smoothly. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis on hover. |

You can adjust the dimensions, colors, or rotation angle to fit your design. Happy coding!
